\">Publish from Cinema 4D (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"publish from houdini (beta)\" href=\"/docs/guides/publish-from-houdini\" id=\"lnk-publish-from-houdini-beta-2\">Publish from Houdini (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"publish from solidworks (beta)\" href=\"/docs/guides/publish-from-solidworks\" id=\"lnk-publish-from-solidworks-beta-2\">Publish from SolidWorks (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"publish from spline, and figma (beta)\" href=\"/docs/guides/publish-from-spline\" id=\"lnk-publish-from-spline-and-figma-beta-2\">Publish from Spline, and Figma (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"camera paths and default walkthroughs\" href=\"/docs/guides/camera-paths\" id=\"lnk-camera-paths-and-default-walkthroughs-2\">Camera paths and default walkthroughs</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"hotspots and doors\" href=\"/docs/guides/hotspots-and-doors\" id=\"lnk-hotspots-and-doors-2\">Hotspots and doors</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse capture: film a room (beta)\" href=\"/docs/guides/film-a-room\" id=\"lnk-verse-capture-film-a-room-beta-2\">Verse Capture: film a room (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse play: host a web game\" href=\"/docs/guides/host-a-web-game\" id=\"lnk-verse-play-host-a-web-game-2\">Verse Play: host a web game</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"spatial bench\" href=\"/docs/guides/spatial-bench\" id=\"lnk-spatial-bench-2\">Spatial Bench</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"light and dark theme\" href=\"/docs/guides/light-and-dark-theme\" id=\"lnk-light-and-dark-theme-2\">Light and dark theme</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"share privately with tokens\" href=\"/docs/guides/share-privately\" id=\"lnk-share-privately-with-tokens-2\">Share privately with tokens</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"show your clients who looked\" href=\"/docs/guides/analytics\" id=\"lnk-show-your-clients-who-looked-2\">Show your clients who looked</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed anywhere: wordpress, shopify, webflow\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-anywhere\" id=\"lnk-embed-anywhere-wordpress-shopify-webflow-2\">Embed anywhere: WordPress, Shopify, Webflow</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse for commerce: 3d on product pages (woocommerce, magento, bigcommerce, salesforce)\" href=\"/docs/guides/commerce\" id=\"lnk-verse-for-commerce-3d-on-product-pages-w-2\">Verse for Commerce: 3D on product pages (WooCommerce, Magento, BigCommerce, Salesforce)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse links and embeds: embed the viewer\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-the-viewer\" id=\"lnk-verse-links-and-embeds-embed-the-viewer-2\">Verse links and embeds: embed the viewer</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"export a flythrough video\" href=\"/docs/guides/export-video\" id=\"lnk-export-a-flythrough-video-2\">Export a flythrough video</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"collect client review comments\" href=\"/docs/guides/collect-review-comments\" id=\"lnk-collect-client-review-comments-2\">Collect client review comments</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"author a guided tour\" href=\"/docs/guides/author-a-guided-tour\" id=\"lnk-author-a-guided-tour-2\">Author a guided tour</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"video on surfaces, sound in the room\" href=\"/docs/guides/video-and-audio\" id=\"lnk-video-on-surfaces-sound-in-the-room-2\">Video on surfaces, sound in the room</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"publish from ifc or usd\" href=\"/docs/guides/publish-from-ifc\" id=\"lnk-publish-from-ifc-or-usd-2\">Publish from IFC or USD</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"upload fbx and obj\" href=\"/docs/guides/upload-fbx-obj\" id=\"lnk-upload-fbx-and-obj-2\">Upload FBX and OBJ</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"build a configurator\" href=\"/docs/guides/build-a-configurator\" id=\"lnk-build-a-configurator-2\">Build a configurator</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"present a scene to a room\" href=\"/docs/guides/present-a-scene\" id=\"lnk-present-a-scene-to-a-room-2\">Present a scene to a room</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse-prepare: the local compression step\" href=\"/docs/guides/verse-prepare\" id=\"lnk-verse-prepare-the-local-compression-step-2\">verse-prepare: the local compression step</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"tune quality knobs\" href=\"/docs/guides/tune-quality\" id=\"lnk-tune-quality-knobs-2\">Tune quality knobs</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"run your own server\" href=\"/docs/guides/run-your-own-server\" id=\"lnk-run-your-own-server-2\">Run your own server</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"monitor production\" href=\"/docs/guides/monitor-production\" id=\"lnk-monitor-production-2\">Monitor production</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"ask verse, the site assistant\" href=\"/docs/guides/ask-verse\" id=\"lnk-ask-verse-the-site-assistant-2\">Ask Verse, the site assistant</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse home: floor plan to 3d home\" href=\"/docs/guides/floor-plan-to-3d\" id=\"lnk-verse-home-floor-plan-to-3d-home-2\">Verse Home: floor plan to 3D home</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse home: plan to a home buyers walk, restyle and tour\" href=\"/docs/guides/instant-home\" id=\"lnk-verse-home-plan-to-a-home-buyers-walk-re-2\">Verse Home: plan to a home buyers walk, restyle and tour</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"&lt;verse-viewer&gt;: one tag, any page\" href=\"/docs/guides/web-component\" id=\"lnk-one-tag-any-page-2\">&lt;verse-viewer&gt;: one tag, any page</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"designer tools: framer, webflow, figma\" href=\"/docs/guides/designer-tools\" id=\"lnk-designer-tools-framer-webflow-figma-2\">Designer tools: Framer, Webflow, Figma</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"react and vue wrappers\" href=\"/docs/guides/react-and-vue\" id=\"lnk-react-and-vue-wrappers-2\">React and Vue wrappers</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"rest client round trip\" href=\"/docs/guides/rest-client\" id=\"lnk-rest-client-round-trip-2\">REST client round trip</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"sell with woocommerce\" href=\"/docs/guides/sell-with-woocommerce\" id=\"lnk-sell-with-woocommerce-2\">Sell with WooCommerce</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"sell with bigcommerce\" href=\"/docs/guides/sell-with-bigcommerce\" id=\"lnk-sell-with-bigcommerce-2\">Sell with BigCommerce</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"sell with magento / adobe commerce\" href=\"/docs/guides/sell-with-magento\" id=\"lnk-sell-with-magento-adobe-commerce-2\">Sell with Magento / Adobe Commerce</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in wix\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-wix\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-wix-2\">Embed in Wix</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in squarespace\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-squarespace\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-squarespace-2\">Embed in Squarespace</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in framer\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-framer\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-framer-2\">Embed in Framer</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in ghost and hubspot\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-ghost-and-hubspot\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-ghost-and-hubspot-2\">Embed in Ghost and HubSpot</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"automate with zapier\" href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-zapier\" id=\"lnk-automate-with-zapier-2\">Automate with Zapier</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"automate with make\" href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-make\" id=\"lnk-automate-with-make-2\">Automate with Make</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"automate with n8n\" href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-n8n\" id=\"lnk-automate-with-n8n-2\">Automate with n8n</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-10\"><h2>Blog & updates</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"all posts\" href=\"/docs/blog/index\" id=\"lnk-all-posts-2\">All posts</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"how verse streams a building\" href=\"/docs/blog/how-verse-streams-a-building\" id=\"lnk-how-verse-streams-a-building-2\">How Verse streams a building</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"2.7: what's new for you\" href=\"/docs/blog/verse-engine-2-7-whats-new\" id=\"lnk-2-7-what-s-new-for-you-2\">2.7: what's new for you</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"2.0 release notes for humans\" href=\"/docs/blog/2-0-release-notes-for-humans\" id=\"lnk-2-0-release-notes-for-humans-2\">2.0 release notes for humans</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-11\"><h2>Integrations</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"integrations: every platform at a glance\" href=\"/docs/integrations\" id=\"lnk-integrations-every-platform-at-a-glance-2\">Integrations: every platform at a glance</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-12\"><h2>API & SDK</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse api, sdk and mcp: embed, sdk, webhooks\" href=\"/docs/developers\" id=\"lnk-verse-api-sdk-and-mcp-embed-sdk-webhooks-2\">Verse API, SDK and MCP: embed, SDK, webhooks</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse api reference\" href=\"/docs/api\" id=\"lnk-verse-api-reference-2\">Verse API reference</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"api quickstart\" href=\"/docs/api-quickstart\" id=\"lnk-api-quickstart-2\">API quickstart</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"api changelog\" href=\"/docs/api-changelog\" id=\"lnk-api-changelog-2\">API changelog</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed sdk reference\" href=\"/docs/embed-sdk\" id=\"lnk-embed-sdk-reference-2\">Embed SDK reference</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse sdk: js / ts (@ctruhtech/verse-sdk)\" href=\"/docs/sdk\" id=\"lnk-verse-sdk-js-ts-ctruhtech-verse-sdk-2\">Verse SDK: JS / TS (@ctruhtech/verse-sdk)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse mcp server for ai agents\" href=\"/docs/mcp\" id=\"lnk-verse-mcp-server-for-ai-agents-2\">Verse MCP server for AI agents</a></section><p class=\"docs-no-results\" hidden>No matching guides.</p></div></nav></aside><div class=\"doc-body\"><article class=\"doc-article\" id=\"art-doc-article\"><h1 id=\"experience-manifests-verse-json\">Experience manifests (<code>.verse.json</code>)<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#experience-manifests-verse-json\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section\">#</a></h1>\n<p>An experience is one JSON file that turns a folder of assets into a walkthrough URL: a base scene, extra GLBs placed into it, lighting, ambience, and the hotspots a buyer jumps between. The playground runs one with <code>?experience=&lt;url&gt;</code>; the embed SDK with <code>viewer.load(&quot;x.verse.json&quot;)</code>. All URLs resolve against the manifest and must be same-origin (the Verse origin never feeds foreign bytes to the parsers).</p>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"json\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-json\">{\n  &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Purvankara 3BHK&quot;,\n  &quot;scene&quot;: &quot;ingest/purvankara-d992a4ef9b5d.vpk&quot;,\n  &quot;props&quot;: [\n    { &quot;url&quot;: &quot;props/sofa.glb&quot;, &quot;position&quot;: [2.1, 0, -1.4], &quot;yaw&quot;: 90, &quot;scale&quot;: 1 }\n  ],\n  &quot;environment&quot;: &quot;env/evening.hdr&quot;,\n  &quot;ambience&quot;: { &quot;particles&quot;: &quot;dust@2,1.5,-1*1&quot;, &quot;audio&quot;: &quot;wind@0,2,0&quot; },\n  &quot;dof&quot;: { &quot;focus&quot;: 3.5, &quot;aperture&quot;: 0 },\n  &quot;exposure&quot;: 0.8,\n  &quot;spawn&quot;: { &quot;position&quot;: [0, 1.6, 3], &quot;yaw&quot;: 180 },\n  &quot;hotspots&quot;: [\n    { &quot;id&quot;: &quot;kitchen&quot;, &quot;label&quot;: &quot;Kitchen&quot;, &quot;position&quot;: [4, 1.6, -2], &quot;look&quot;: [4, 1.2, -6],\n      &quot;anchor&quot;: [4, 1.0, -5.5], &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Kitchen&quot;, &quot;body&quot;: &quot;Island in **quartz**, [brochure](https://…)&quot;,\n      &quot;image&quot;: &quot;/ingest/poster-9a1b2c3d4e.png&quot;, &quot;link&quot;: &quot;https://example.com/kitchen&quot; }\n  ],\n  &quot;tour&quot;: {\n    &quot;steps&quot;: [\n      { &quot;hotspot&quot;: &quot;kitchen&quot;, &quot;eye&quot;: [4, 1.6, -2], &quot;look&quot;: [4, 1.2, -6], &quot;dwell&quot;: 4,\n        &quot;narration&quot;: &quot;The kitchen opens onto the terrace.&quot;, &quot;audio&quot;: &quot;/ingest/exp-38fd878a72-media-9a1b2c3d.mp3&quot; }\n    ]\n  },\n  &quot;sun&quot;: { &quot;azimuth&quot;: 150, &quot;elevation&quot;: 30, &quot;intensity&quot;: 3 },\n  &quot;version&quot;: 2\n}</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>scene</code> (required unless <code>scenes</code>)</td><td><code>.vpk</code> streams through the meshlet DAG; <code>.glb</code>/<code>.gltf</code> loads whole. Loads first; everything else waits for it.</td></tr><tr><td><code>scenes</code></td><td>up to 8 <code>{url, position, yaw, scale}</code> streamed objects in one experience (apartment + clubhouse). The first is the base — camera framing and the walk grid come from it; the rest stream additively at their world offsets, rotated <code>yaw</code> degrees about +Y. The playground&#39;s URL-knob twin is <code>?vpk=&lt;base&gt;&amp;vpk2=url@x,y,z*yawDeg*scale;url@…</code> — each <code>;</code>-separated entry places one extra <code>.vpk</code> (<code>@x,y,z</code> offset in metres, <code>*yawDeg</code> rotation, <code>*scale</code> uniform; all optional, defaults <code>0,0,0</code> / <code>0</code> / <code>1</code>).</td></tr><tr><td><code>props</code></td><td>Up to 64 GLBs appended to the scene after it reports in. <code>position</code> metres, <code>yaw</code> degrees about +Y, <code>scale</code> uniform. Props are static (their own animations, skins and morphs are ignored in v1) and do not join the walk-collision grid.</td></tr><tr><td><code>environment</code></td><td>An <code>.hdr</code> on this origin, applied as the image-based light.</td></tr><tr><td><code>ambience</code></td><td>The <code>?particles=</code> / <code>?audio=</code> knob strings: <code>kind@x,y,z*scale;…</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>dof</code></td><td>Depth of field: focus distance (m) and aperture (px·m, 0 = off). Tiers A/B.</td></tr><tr><td><code>exposure</code></td><td>EV stops applied in linear space before the tonemap, clamped ±4; omitted = default look (0 EV). Authored via the editor&#39;s Exposure slider, applied on load through the same <code>set-exposure</code> verb as <code>?exposure=</code> and the embed&#39;s <code>setExposure(ev)</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>spawn</code></td><td>Where walk mode starts: eye position + yaw. Replaces the occupancy-derived spawn search.</td></tr><tr><td><code>start</code></td><td>Optional, 4.0: <code>&quot;walk&quot;</code> opens the visitor standing at <code>spawn</code> in walk mode once the scene has loaded (generated floor-plan homes use it). Absent = the scene&#39;s own opening camera.</td></tr><tr><td><code>hotspots</code></td><td>Up to 64 <code>{id, label, position, look}</code>. A jump enters walk mode at <code>position</code> facing <code>look</code>, so the collision walk continues from there. <strong>Version 2</strong> adds the pin and its card: <code>anchor</code> (the surface point the numbered pin hangs on — defaults to <code>position</code>), <code>title</code> (120 chars), <code>body</code> (2000 chars of plain text with <code>**bold**</code>, <code>*italic*</code> and <code>[text](https://…)</code> links), <code>image</code> (same-origin URL) and <code>link</code> (http/https). A hotspot with any of these renders as a pin + info card instead of the v1 button strip.</td></tr><tr><td><code>tour</code></td><td>Version 2: the guided tour — <code>steps</code> (up to 64) of <code>{hotspot?, eye, look, dwell, narration?, audio?}</code>. <code>eye</code>/<code>look</code> are the camera pose (defaults: the named hotspot&#39;s <code>position</code>/<code>look</code>); <code>dwell</code> seconds the camera rests there (0.5–60, default 4); <code>narration</code> text (2000 chars, same rich-text subset) and <code>audio</code> a same-origin clip (<code>POST /v1/experience/&lt;id&gt;/media</code>, ≤ 2 MB). Playback flies between steps at ~2 m/s (≥ 1.2 s a leg) on the engine&#39;s camera path, shows the narration per step, and leaves the walker standing at the last step. Steps whose <code>eye</code> cannot be resolved are dropped; an empty list reads as no tour.</td></tr><tr><td><code>sun</code></td><td>Version 2: <code>{azimuth, elevation, intensity}</code> in the engine&#39;s S5 convention (degrees; azimuth from +X toward +Z, elevation 2–90, intensity 0–20, default 2.8) — the same triple as <code>?sun=</code> and the embed&#39;s <code>setSun</code>. Applied on load; a <code>?sun=</code> knob in the link still wins because it applies after.</td></tr><tr><td><code>exterior</code></td><td>2.7: the exterior kit&#39;s state — <code>{ sky: {on, turbidity, exposure, clouds: {coverage, density}}, weather: {kind, intensity, wind}, fog: {on, density, height, falloff, colour}, ground: {kind, size, material, y, colour, heightfield, amplitude, center} }</code> (every field optional; the viewer fills defaults and clamps). <code>ground.heightfield</code> is the scene&#39;s <code>ingest/&lt;id&gt;.ground.png</code>. The Author bar writes it when &quot;Save the exterior&quot; is ticked; share-string knobs in the link win because they apply after.</td></tr><tr><td><code>lights</code></td><td>2.7.2: the light studio&#39;s share string (<code>all=1.2;env=1.5;ev=0.8;soft=3;l0=…;e3=…</code>, see <code>lights.js</code>), written by <strong>Make it look good</strong> for a signed-in owner and applied with <code>sun</code> / <code>exterior</code> when the manifest mounts; a <code>?lights=</code> on the link wins because it applies after.</td></tr><tr><td><code>version</code></td><td><code>2</code> for manifests carrying the keys above; absent/<code>1</code> reads exactly as before (no pins, no tour, no sun). The parser never rejects a version it does not know — unknown keys are ignored.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Runtime contract: the <code>experience</code> event fires when the manifest is parsed; <code>loaded</code> when the base scene is up; each prop that fails leaves the rest loading and reports through <code>error</code>. On GPU-context recovery the engine replays the base GLB and its props itself; a streamed base is re-streamed by the worker.</p>\n<p>Authoring (2.7): the playground&#39;s <code>?author=1</code> <strong>Author bar</strong> (a signed-in Studio session; <a href=\"/docs/guides/author-a-guided-tour\" id=\"lnk-guide\">guide</a>) writes version-2 manifests — click a surface to drop a hotspot (the pick lands <code>anchor</code>, the current view becomes <code>position</code>/<code>look</code>), reorder, fill the card, record a tour step per hotspot (pose from the current view, dwell, narration, audio), keep the sun — and saves through <code>POST /v1/experience</code> then <code>PUT /v1/experience/&lt;id&gt;</code>; &quot;Set as link default&quot; (<code>PUT /v1/scenes/&lt;id&gt;/experience</code>) makes the plain share link <code>/?vpk=ingest/&lt;id&gt;.vpk</code> play it. Viewers and embeds read edited manifests through <code>GET /v1/experience/&lt;id&gt;</code> (<code>?experience=/v1/experience/&lt;id&gt;</code>), never the year-immutable static copy. Studio lists a scene&#39;s experiences under <strong>Experiences</strong>.</p>\n<p>The playground&#39;s <code>?edit=1</code> editor writes these manifests — capture spawn/hotspots from the camera, tap to place props and ambience, then Download or Publish (<code>POST /v1/experience</code> → <code>ingest/exp-&lt;id&gt;.verse.json</code> + share link). Manifests publish with root-relative URLs so they resolve from <code>ingest/</code>. The Scenes section authors <code>scenes</code> directly: add streamed <code>.vpk</code> objects at x/y/z/yaw/scale offsets with immediate additive preview; the base scene becomes entry 0 on export, and removing a scene — like removing a prop — re-previews on reload. 📸 Poster captures the viewport and publishes it (<code>POST /v1/poster</code> → <code>ingest/poster-&lt;id&gt;.png</code>) for the embed&#39;s <code>data-poster</code>.</p>\n<p>Auto-staging: ingest scenes compiled with a walk-collision grid ship <code>ingest/&lt;id&gt;.stage.json</code> (a compiler-picked <code>spawn</code> in exactly this manifest&#39;s format, plus a 20–60 s auto tour in the <code>/v1/tour</code> sample format, planned through free space on the collision grid for interiors) and <code>ingest/&lt;id&gt;.plan.svg</code> (a deterministic floor plan the minimap uses as its base layer) — see <code>docs/api.md</code>. The <code>?edit=1</code> editor seeds its draft spawn from the stage manifest and shows &quot;Auto-staged ✓&quot;; an explicit <code>spawn</code> here always wins over the auto one.</p>\n<p>Not yet: gizmo manipulation of placed items and scenes (offsets are numeric); walk grids of SCALED scene placements (translation + yaw grids contribute; scale sits out of collision).</p></article><div class=\"doc-source\">Published documentation from <a href=\"https://verse.ctruh.com/docs/#/experience-format\" id=\"lnk-verse-by-ctruh\">Verse by Ctruh</a></div></div></section>"}